<!--META-DATA
{
	"tags": ["monte-carlo", "dice", "poker", "simulation", "function", "confidence-interval", "table"]
}
-->

<statement>
	<p>
		This function estimates the probabilities of all 5-dice poker hand types via Monte Carlo simulation and displays a confidence-interval summary table.
	</p>

	<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
		<col width="12%"/>
		<col width="88%" halign="left"/>

		<row>
			<cell><p>Inputs:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>trials</pf> (1 x 1) integer — number of 5-dice rolls to simulate. Default: <m>10^6</m> when omitted.</p>
				<p><pf>seed</pf> (optional, 1 x 1 integer) — random number generator seed for reproducibility.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell><p>Outputs:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p>Displays a MATLAB table for each hand type with columns:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><pf>varNames</pf> — hand type name.</li>
					<li><pf>varCounts</pf> — simulated count across all trials.</li>
					<li><pf>pHat</pf> — proportion estimate (rounded to four decimals).</li>
					<li><pf>pct</pf> — percentage formatting of <pf>pHat</pf>.</li>
					<li><pf>marginErr</pf> — 95% margin of error (± percentage).</li>
					<li><pf>confLvl</pf> — reported confidence level.</li>
				</ul>
				<p><em>Note:</em> This function prints the table to the Command Window and does not return an output variable.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row>
			<cell><p>Hand types:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p>The simulation tallies the following ranks (as ordered in the output):</p>
				<ul>
					<li>5 of a kind</li>
					<li>4 of a kind</li>
					<li>full house</li>
					<li>straight (1-2-3-4-5 or 2-3-4-5-6)</li>
					<li>3 of a kind (not a full house)</li>
					<li>2 pair</li>
					<li>1 pair</li>
					<li>singles (all distinct, not a straight)</li>
				</ul>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row>
			<cell><p>Details:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p>▸ For each trial, generate one roll of five fair dice with <pf>randi(6,1,5)</pf>.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row>
			<cell/>
			<cell><p>▸ Compute face counts with <pf>get_face_counts</pf>, sort the roll by rank using <pf>sort_by_rank</pf>, then determine the rank ID <pf>rid</pf> via <pf>get_rank</pf>.</p></cell>
		</row>

		<row>
			<cell/>
			<cell><p>▸ Accumulate counts per rank over all <pf>trials</pf>. After simulation, call <pf>confidence_interval_table</pf> with a 95% confidence level to display estimates and intervals.</p></cell>
		</row>

		<row>
			<cell/>
			<cell><p>▸ The function temporarily adds <pf>'../dice-poker-struct'</pf> to the MATLAB path to access helper functions and removes it afterward.</p></cell>
		</row>

		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell><p>Notes:</p></cell>
			<cell>
				<p>▸ If <pf>seed</pf> is provided, the simulation initializes with <pf>rng(seed,'twister')</pf> for reproducibility.</p>
				<p>▸ Larger <pf>trials</pf> reduce Monte Carlo sampling error; margins of error in the table are computed assuming a normal approximation (via the 95% z-score).</p>
			</cell>
		</row>

		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell><p>Helpers:</p></cell>
			<cell><p><pf>get_face_counts</pf>, <pf>sort_by_rank</pf>, <pf>get_rank</pf>, <pf>confidence_interval_table</pf></p></cell>
		</row>
	</tabular>

	<p>
		Examples:
		<program>
			<code>
				% Example 1: Quick estimate (small simulation)
				mc_dice_poker_roll_probs(1e5, 123)
				% Displays a 95% CI table for all 8 hand types.
			</code>
		</program>
		<program>
			<code>
				% Example 2: Use default trials (1e6) without a seed
				mc_dice_poker_roll_probs()
				% Displays a higher-precision table (longer runtime).
			</code>
		</program>
	</p>
</statement>
